# Two attackers in the same combat, only one of them blocked: Grizzly Bears
# (2/2) and Silvercoat Lion (2/2) both attack ai, whose lone Hill Giant
# (3/3) blocks only the Bears -- the Lion goes through unblocked. Each
# attacker's own exchange in dealCombatDamageStep is independent (keyed by
# attacker, combatdamage.go's own per-attacker loop), so the Lion hitting ai
# directly and the Bears trading with the Giant are two separate outcomes in
# the same damage step, not a single combined one.
startturn human
advance 5
queue attackers 1,2
declareattackers
advance
queue blocks 3=1
declareblockers
advance
advance
combatdamage
advance
